-- title:
--   Ends and smooth-point stalks from an affine chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for an extension $F/K$ a *place* (`Place K F`) is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, and a principal ideal ring; `Place.ord` is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb Z^{m0}$-valued adic valuation, `Place.IsRational` says that $K$ surjects onto the residue field of the place, and `Place.evalAt f` is the element of $K$ corresponding to the residue of $f$ when $f$ lies in the valuation subring (and $0$ otherwise). A `RegularProlongation A F Fbar` consists of a valuation subring `integers` of $F$ whose intersection with the base field is $A$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism to `Fbar` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ can be scaled by a base constant into `integers` with nonzero residue.
--
--   The data are: a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime q`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field $\kappa(A)$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'` — whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, the rational places that are affine geometric and at which the value of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`; the hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of the Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $M'$) is contained in `fieldBar q M'` (the analogous $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield attached to the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$); and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   The base is described by: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), henselian (`hhens`), with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`) and algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the hypothesis `hκ` that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; the hypothesis `halgc` that $\kappa(A)$ is algebraically closed; an algebra structure $\mathbb F_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2` $\to \kappa(A)$; the hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa(A)[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q … - 1`) is a domain; an index `ζix : Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and, in intermediate-field form, $K_b$ with $K_b = \bot$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $A_b = A \cap K_b$ (`hAb`), which is a discrete valuation ring, henselian, with maximal ideal generated by a nonzero element $\varpi_b$.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying: the compositum of the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and the linear-disjointness hypothesis that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$ over $k_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   Further, for every subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and every $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` on $B$ subject to the following affine-chart hypotheses: the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $a$ viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $B$ is contained in the compositum $L :=$ `adjoin k₀ (image of Kb) ⊔ F₀`; every element of $L$ is a fraction $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ with image in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is exactly the set of $f \in F_0$ of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; the element of `fieldBar q M'` obtained from the $q$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the modular invariant, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` and included via `hle`, lies in $B$; and for every $\zeta :$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $B$ into $B$.
--
--   The last hypothesis on $B$ (the special-fibre hypothesis) requires that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa(A)$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta :$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the fraction field of the Drinfeld coordinate ring of the subgroup generated by the actions `hFunctionFieldAction` at the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that: $\mathrm{card}(C_s) = 2\,\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, where the latter is `jWidthChar q` evaluated at the value of `jGeomGen` at $s$, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` (the order of vanishing at $s$ of `jGeomGen` minus its value); the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by $\kappa(A) \to$ `quotField …`; every element of `quotField …` is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose image in `drinfeldFunctionField q (ResidueField A)` lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and $\rho$ is equivariant in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma, 1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,u) \mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the value $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f)$ equals `hFunctionFieldAction` at $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, as elements of the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Under all of this, for every field $F_{ss}$ with a $\kappa(A)$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` with residue field $F_{ss}$ such that an element of $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` precisely when it lies in $W_0$, the following holds. There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$, and, indexed by the places $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$, subrings $S_Q$ of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[T] \to S_Q$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa(A)$ and sets $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that:
--
--   (i) $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   (ii) For every $Q \notin N$: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is that image, for every $a \in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; $S_Q$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the kernel of $\chi_Q$; $S_Q$ is contained in the compositum $L$; every element of $L$ is a fraction of two elements of $S_Q$ with nonzero denominator; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in `R.integers`, and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` if and only if $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$ divides it in $S_Q$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the residue $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue at $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa(A) \to$ `Q.ResidueField`; $\varphi_Q(T)$ lies in `R.integers` and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its residue equals $1$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are rational, such that every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and such that for every $f \in S_Q$ the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ has $A$-valuation $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   (iii) The sets $D_Q$, for $Q \notin N$, are pairwise disjoint: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   (iv) For $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the order at $P$ of the element of `fieldBar q M'` coming from the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant is non-negative.
--
--   (v) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta :$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof $h_\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, writing $\bar\tau =$ `R.resAut τ hτ` for the induced $\kappa(A)$-automorphism of $F_{ss}$: for every place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$, $\bar\tau \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$; and if $Q \notin N$, then `smulDisc τ (Db Q)` $= \{P \mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_Q\}$ equals $D_{\bar\tau \cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the smooth-point half of the analysis of the supersingular component of a semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$: from an affine chart $B$ over $A_b$ whose special fibre is an affine quotient Drinfeld curve, it produces the $q+1$ ends, and, at each remaining place of the special fibre, a local stalk with an étale coordinate, its residue character and its residue disc, all equivariant for the level automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks), and cites the companion results `supersingularProlongation_residue_surjective_ker_of_affineChart`, `supersingularProlongation_ends_of_affineChart`, `supersingularProlongation_smoothPointStalk_of_affineChart` and `supersingularProlongation_discRiders_of_affineChart`, together with [`RingHom.exists_algEquiv_comp_eq_of_ker_eq_of_forall_exists_mul_eq`](thm.html#RingHom.exists_algEquiv_comp_eq_of_ker_eq_of_forall_exists_mul_eq) identifying $F_{ss}$ with the quotient Drinfeld function field.
